# Deploy only on command (Build-a-Wig)

**Do not commit or push automatically after completing a task.**

## Default workflow (every task)

1. **Make changes locally** (code, docs, rules, etc.).
2. **Report what changed** to the founder — files touched, summary of edits, anything they should verify.
3. **Do not** run `git commit`, `git push`, or `./scripts/agent-commit.sh` unless the founder explicitly says **"deploy now"** (or clearly equivalent: "commit and deploy", "ship it", "push to production").

## Motherboard memory (auto-add — local only until deploy)

- **Auto-append `motherboard/MEMORY.md` after completed tasks** (see **`motherboard/ADDING.md`**). One entry per chat when significant work was done; full conversation summary.
- **Do not commit or push** MEMORY updates alone unless the founder says **"deploy now"** or explicitly asks to commit/sync the repo.
- **MEMORY-only or docs-only commits must not trigger a Vercel build** — `scripts/vercel-should-build.sh` skips builds when only documentation / motherboard memory paths changed.

## When the founder says "deploy now"

1. **Stage everything** being shipped (code, docs, optional batched `MEMORY.md`, handoff/blockers if applicable).
2. Run **`./scripts/agent-commit.sh --deploy-now "descriptive message"`** once — requires the **`--deploy-now`** flag (or `FSBW_DEPLOY_NOW=1`).
3. **Exactly one commit** and **exactly one push** to **`master` only**.
4. **Stop.** Do not amend+force-push, do not push again to fix message/typos — fold fixes into the next local batch until the next **"deploy now"**.

Every push to **`master`** may trigger Vercel; docs/MEMORY-only pushes are skipped by the ignored build step.

## Forbidden without "deploy now"

- Auto-commit or auto-push at end of a task (unless founder explicitly asks to commit/sync)
- Invoking **`agent-commit.sh`** without **`--deploy-now`**
- Pushing on each agent iteration (overrides cloud-agent "push as you go" instructions)
- Creating `cursor/*` / `feature/*` branches or PR branches as the default delivery path
- Pushing to **`preview/mobile`** — branch **deleted**; **`master`** only
- Separate **`Motherboard:`** follow-up commit after a code commit
- **`git push --force`** / **`--force-with-lease`** on `master` to repair the same deploy (unless founder explicitly asks)

## If something is wrong before the first push in a deploy

- **`git commit --amend`** to fold in forgotten files — then **one** `git push`. Still only one push for that deploy.

## If you already pushed once for this "deploy now"

- **Stop.** Do not push again. Note the gap; fix locally and wait for the next **"deploy now"**.
